\toc3 Mal
\mt1 MALACHI
\c 1
\p \v 1 The burden of the word of the LORD to Israel by Malachi.
\v 2 I have loved you, said the LORD. Yet you say, Wherein have you loved us? \add Was\add* not Esau Jacob's brother? said the LORD: yet I loved Jacob,
\v 3 And I hated Esau, and laid his mountains and his heritage waste for the dragons of the wilderness.
\v 4 Whereas Edom said, We are impoverished, but we will return and build the desolate places; thus said the LORD of hosts, They shall build, but I will throw down; and they shall call them, The border of wickedness, and, The people against whom the LORD has indignation for ever.
\v 5 And your eyes shall see, and you shall say, The LORD will be magnified from the border of Israel.
\v 6 A son honors \add his\add* father, and a servant his master: if then I \add be\add* a father, where \add is\add* my honor? and if I \add be\add* a master, where \add is\add* my fear? said the LORD of hosts to you, O priests, that despise my name. And you say, Wherein have we despised your name?
\v 7 You offer polluted bread on my altar; and you say, Wherein have we polluted you? In that you say, The table of the LORD \add is\add* contemptible.
\v 8 And if you offer the blind for sacrifice, \add is it\add* not evil? and if you offer the lame and sick, \add is it\add* not evil? offer it now to your governor; will he be pleased with you, or accept your person? said the LORD of hosts.
\v 9 And now, I pray you, beseech God that he will be gracious to us: this has been by your means: will he regard your persons? said the LORD of hosts.
\v 10 Who \add is there\add* even among you that would shut the doors \add for nothing\add*? neither do you kindle \add fire\add* on my altar for nothing. I have no pleasure in you, said the LORD of hosts, neither will I accept an offering at your hand.
\v 11 For from the rising of the sun even to the going down of the same my name \add shall be\add* great among the Gentiles; and in every place incense \add shall be\add* offered to my name, and a pure offering: for my name \add shall be\add* great among the heathen, said the LORD of hosts.
\v 12 But you have profaned it, in that you say, The table of the LORD \add is\add* polluted; and the fruit thereof, \add even\add* his meat, \add is\add* contemptible.
\v 13 You said also, Behold, what a weariness \add is it\add*! and you have snuffed at it, said the LORD of hosts; and you brought \add that which was\add* torn, and the lame, and the sick; thus you brought an offering: should I accept this of your hand? said the LORD.
\v 14 But cursed \add be\add* the deceiver, which has in his flock a male, and vows, and sacrifices to the LORD a corrupt thing: for I \add am\add* a great King, said the LORD of hosts, and my name \add is\add* dreadful among the heathen.
\c 2
\p \v 1 And now, O you priests, this commandment \add is\add* for you.
\v 2 If you will not hear, and if you will not lay \add it\add* to heart, to give glory to my name, said the LORD of hosts, I will even send a curse on you, and I will curse your blessings: yes, I have cursed them already, because you do not lay \add it\add* to heart.
\v 3 Behold, I will corrupt your seed, and spread dung on your faces, \add even\add* the dung of your solemn feasts; and \add one\add* shall take you away with it.
\v 4 And you shall know that I have sent this commandment to you, that my covenant might be with Levi, said the LORD of hosts.
\v 5 My covenant was with him of life and peace; and I gave them to him \add for\add* the fear with which he feared me, and was afraid before my name.
\v 6 The law of truth was in his mouth, and iniquity was not found in his lips: he walked with me in peace and equity, and did turn many away from iniquity.
\v 7 For the priest's lips should keep knowledge, and they should seek the law at his mouth: for he \add is\add* the messenger of the LORD of hosts.
\v 8 But you are departed out of the way; you have caused many to stumble at the law; you have corrupted the covenant of Levi, said the LORD of hosts.
\v 9 Therefore have I also made you contemptible and base before all the people, according as you have not kept my ways, but have been partial in the law.
\v 10 Have we not all one father? has not one God created us? why do we deal treacherously every man against his brother, by profaning the covenant of our fathers?
\v 11 Judah has dealt treacherously, and an abomination is committed in Israel and in Jerusalem; for Judah has profaned the holiness of the LORD which he loved, and has married the daughter of a strange god.
\v 12 The LORD will cut off the man that does this, the master and the scholar, out of the tabernacles of Jacob, and him that offers an offering to the LORD of hosts.
\v 13 And this have you done again, covering the altar of the LORD with tears, with weeping, and with crying out, so that he regards not the offering any more, or receives \add it\add* with good will at your hand.
\v 14 Yet you say, Why? Because the LORD has been witness between you and the wife of your youth, against whom you have dealt treacherously: yet \add is\add* she your companion, and the wife of your covenant.
\v 15 And did not he make one? Yet had he the residue of the spirit. And why one? That he might seek a godly seed. Therefore take heed to your spirit, and let none deal treacherously against the wife of his youth.
\v 16 For the LORD, the God of Israel, said that he hates putting away: for \add one\add* covers violence with his garment, said the LORD of hosts: therefore take heed to your spirit, that you deal not treacherously.
\v 17 You have wearied the LORD with your words. Yet you say, Wherein have we wearied \add him\add*? When you say, Every one that does evil \add is\add* good in the sight of the LORD, and he delights in them; or, Where \add is\add* the God of judgment?
\c 3
\p \v 1 Behold, I will send my messenger, and he shall prepare the way before me: and the LORD, whom you seek, shall suddenly come to his temple, even the messenger of the covenant, whom you delight in: behold, he shall come, said the LORD of hosts.
\v 2 But who may abide the day of his coming? and who shall stand when he appears? for he \add is\add* like a refiner's fire, and like fullers' soap:
\v 3 And he shall sit \add as\add* a refiner and purifier of silver: and he shall purify the sons of Levi, and purge them as gold and silver, that they may offer to the LORD an offering in righteousness.
\v 4 Then shall the offering of Judah and Jerusalem be pleasant to the LORD, as in the days of old, and as in former years.
\v 5 And I will come near to you to judgment; and I will be a swift witness against the sorcerers, and against the adulterers, and against false swearers, and against those that oppress the hireling in \add his\add* wages, the widow, and the fatherless, and that turn aside the stranger \add from his right\add*, and fear not me, said the LORD of hosts.
\v 6 For I \add am\add* the LORD, I change not; therefore you sons of Jacob are not consumed.
\v 7 Even from the days of your fathers you are gone away from my ordinances, and have not kept \add them\add*. Return to me, and I will return to you, said the LORD of hosts. But you said, Wherein shall we return?
\v 8 Will a man rob God? Yet you have robbed me. But you say, Wherein have we robbed you? In tithes and offerings.
\v 9 You \add are\add* cursed with a curse: for you have robbed me, \add even\add* this whole nation.
\v 10 Bring you all the tithes into the storehouse, that there may be meat in my house, and prove me now herewith, said the LORD of hosts, if I will not open you the windows of heaven, and pour you out a blessing, that \add there shall\add* not \add be room\add* enough \add to receive it\add*.
\v 11 And I will rebuke the devourer for your sakes, and he shall not destroy the fruits of your ground; neither shall your vine cast her fruit before the time in the field, said the LORD of hosts.
\v 12 And all nations shall call you blessed: for you shall be a delightsome land, said the LORD of hosts.
\v 13 Your words have been stout against me, said the LORD. Yet you say, What have we spoken \add so much\add* against you?
\v 14 You have said, It \add is\add* vain to serve God: and what profit \add is it\add* that we have kept his ordinance, and that we have walked mournfully before the LORD of hosts?
\v 15 And now we call the proud happy; yes, they that work wickedness are set up; yes, \add they that\add* tempt God are even delivered.
\v 16 Then they that feared the LORD spoke often one to another: and the LORD listened, and heard \add it\add*, and a book of remembrance was written before him for them that feared the LORD, and that thought on his name.
\v 17 And they shall be mine, said the LORD of hosts, in that day when I make up my jewels; and I will spare them, as a man spares his own son that serves him.
\v 18 Then shall you return, and discern between the righteous and the wicked, between him that serves God and him that serves him not.
\c 4
\p \v 1 For, behold, the day comes, that shall burn as an oven; and all the proud, yes, and all that do wickedly, shall be stubble: and the day that comes shall burn them up, said the LORD of hosts, that it shall leave them neither root nor branch.
\v 2 But to you that fear my name shall the Sun of righteousness arise with healing in his wings; and you shall go forth, and grow up as calves of the stall.
\v 3 And you shall tread down the wicked; for they shall be ashes under the soles of your feet in the day that I shall do \add this\add*, said the LORD of hosts.
\v 4 Remember you the law of Moses my servant, which I commanded to him in Horeb for all Israel, \add with\add* the statutes and judgments.
\v 5 Behold, I will send you Elijah the prophet before the coming of the great and dreadful day of the LORD:
\v 6 And he shall turn the heart of the fathers to the children, and the heart of the children to their fathers, lest I come and smite the earth with a curse.
